## Multi-Tenant Architecture Overview

The keycloak-alpha platform uses **shared database, single collection** approach with org_id-based isolation:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│          Keycloak (Identity Provider)        │
│  - Manages users across all organizations   │
│  - Issues JWT tokens with org_id claim      │
│  - Handles authentication & SSO             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    ↓ JWT with org_id
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│            API Gateway                       │
│  - Validates tokens                         │
│  - Extracts org_id claim                    │
│  - Routes to microservices                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    ↓ org_id in headers
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Microservices (8 services)          │
│  - Enforce org_id filtering                 │
│  - Isolate data by organization             │
│  - Apply org-specific business logic        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│    MongoDB                                  │
│  - Shared database                          │
│  - org_id indexed on all collections        │
│  - Document-level security                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

